## Task

For every `change_plan.files[]` entry, check the file on disk:

1. `created` / `modified`: the file exists and implements `summary`.
2. `deleted`: the file is gone and nothing references it.
3. Changes outside the plan's files are findings (scope creep).

Skip anything in the lint list.

## Untrusted source: lint findings

```text
{% for f in input.lint_findings %}
- {{ f.file_line }} — {{ f.title }}
{% else %}
- (none)
{% endfor %}
```

## Output

```bash
LOOM={{ input.__loom.runtime }}
WD={{ input.__loom.workdir }}
$LOOM output init "$WD" --task '{{ input.__task.id }}'
$LOOM output add "$WD" --task '{{ input.__task.id }}' \
    --set 'findings[].title=<short>' \
    --set 'findings[-1].file_line=<path>:<line>' \
    --set 'findings[-1].description=<what differs from the plan>' \
    --set 'findings[-1].fix=<concrete change>' \
    --set 'findings[-1].severity=Error' \
    --set 'findings[-1].source={{ input.__task.id }}'
```

No findings: `--set-json 'findings=[]'`.
